; Background supply-chain guard: npm resolves only versions published at least 7 days ago,
; so a compromised release can be pulled before it is ever picked. Lockfile-driven installs
; (`npm ci`, `npm install` with a satisfying lock) are unaffected — measured 2026-09-02 in
; docs/reviews/2026-09-02-supply-chain-background-guards-completion-report.md.
min-release-age=7

; Supply-chain control: a dependency may run install-time lifecycle scripts
; (preinstall/install/postinstall) only if the workspace policy names it.
; Anything else fails `npm ci` closed with ESTRICTALLOWSCRIPTS before a single
; script runs.
;
; This workspace's allowlist lives in package.json#allowScripts, NOT in this file.
; `npm run` exports .npmrc config to children as npm_config_*, and a nested
; `npm ci` (this tree runs one via `tooling:ci`) then reads allow-scripts from the
; ENV layer, which npm treats as a command-line policy and refuses outright:
; `EALLOWSCRIPTS: --allow-scripts is not allowed in project-scoped installs`.
; It fails before `--ignore-scripts` is considered. Measured 2026-09-02, after it
; broke build:n8n-nodes, test:n8n-nodes and scan:n8n-nodes.
;
; The policy mirrors this workspace lockfile exactly and is enforced by
; scripts/tests/check-npm-install-script-policy.test.mjs (npm run test:meta),
; which also fails if an allowlist reappears here. See
; docs/plans/2026-09-02-npm-install-script-allowlist-hardening.md

strict-allow-scripts=true
